---
import CaseStudy from "../components/CaseStudy.astro";
const summary = "For most wealth management firms, custodial data lives with third-party providers like BridgeFT — not inside Salesforce. That data syncs nightly into Data Cloud, but Data Cloud is a compute engine, not a CRM, and raw custodial records do not map cleanly to FSC's financial data model. Integration Hub solves this in two layers: an out-of-the-box four-step connection wizard that any admin can configure, and a human-in-the-loop Reconciliation Workspace where unmatched records are reviewed, validated, and committed by a real person before they enter the CRM.";
const bullets = [
  "Four-step admin connection wizard (Connect, Map, Configure, Activate) that establishes custodial data integration without custom development — fully out of the box",
  "100% determinism threshold as a design principle: only records matched with full confidence are auto-linked; everything below that threshold routes to the Reconciliation queue for human review",
  "Cascading auto-link reduces review fatigue — when a household-level record is confirmed, all child holdings auto-resolve, collapsing dozens of queue items into a single human decision",
  "Operational truth as a data governance stance: when a human edits a matched record in FSC, that edit persists through future custodial syncs; human judgment outranks the data feed",
];
const sections = [
  { heading: "Integration Hub sets it up. The Reconciliation Workspace makes it trustworthy.", body: "These are two distinct products with two distinct users — the firm administrator who connects and configures the custodial data pipeline, and the operations professional who reviews and validates unmatched records before they enter the CRM. Designing them as separate surfaces with separate interaction models was a deliberate architectural choice: the person who sets up the system should not be the same surface as the person who operates it every day." },
  { heading: "Below 100% confidence, every record gets a human decision point.", body: "The Reconciliation Workspace is not a bulk-approve queue — it is a structured review surface where each unmatched record presents the custodial data alongside the proposed FSC match, with enough context for a human to confirm or override. The 100% determinism threshold means the system never silently links an uncertain record; every ambiguous match waits in the queue until a person decides. That decision is logged, auditable, and permanent." },
  { heading: "When a human edits a record, the edit wins. Every time.", body: "Operational truth is the data governance principle that prevents the system from overwriting human judgment with the next nightly sync. If an advisor or operations professional manually corrects a custodial record in FSC, that correction persists through future data feeds. The custodial data is the source; the human decision is the authority." },
];
const takeaways = [
  "Two-layer architecture is the correct design for any system where setup and operation have different users, different cadences, and different risk profiles. Building one surface for both introduces confusion that no amount of UX polish can fix.",
  "The empty state 'You're all caught up' is a first-class design deliverable. When the Reconciliation queue is empty, the system should confirm that explicitly. The emotional payoff for doing the work is part of the design.",
  "Human-in-the-loop at the 100% confidence threshold is not a hedge — it is the correct design stance for financial data that will influence advisor decisions and client reporting. The cost of a silent error is higher than the cost of a human review queue.",
  "Cascading auto-link is the design feature that makes determinism feel fast rather than slow. One household confirmation resolves every child holding without additional clicks. Efficiency is preserved; oversight is not sacrificed.",
];
---
<CaseStudy
  title="Integration Hub"
  eyebrow="Salesforce"
  role="Senior Product Designer"
  year="2024–2025"
  summary={summary}
  bullets={bullets}
  sections={sections}
  takeaways={takeaways}
  imageStart={37}
  prevCase={{ title: "Advisor Anywhere", href: "/advisor-anywhere", eyebrow: "Salesforce FSC" }}
  nextCase={{ title: "Wealth Agents", href: "/wealth-agents", eyebrow: "Salesforce FSC" }}
/>
